1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,060
It's not a date, is it?

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:05,210
With whom?

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:06,460
Huh?

4
00:00:13,021 --> 00:00:15,601
So, you like this stuff, Sui?

5
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,800
Yeah.

6
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:25,710
Dai-chan, what do you want?

7
00:00:26,430 --> 00:00:29,420
You didn't run away like this before.

8
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:31,750
Who are you meeting for the date?

9
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:36,120
W-Well...

10
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,082
Harutora?

11
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:42,242
Wait, H-Harutora?

12
00:00:42,242 --> 00:00:43,640
Hey!

13
00:00:46,307 --> 00:00:47,747
Harutora?

14
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:07,290
S-Stop it!

15
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,480
Why are you showing him your weak side?

16
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,397
I... I didn't mean to.

17
00:01:19,397 --> 00:01:21,310
That's not how it looked to me.

18
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:26,278
It's true. Even I've always hated
that side of Dai-chan...

19
00:01:26,278 --> 00:01:27,898
If that's true...

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,990
What about when he was in your room?

21
00:01:31,990 --> 00:01:37,090
That's because my roommate
used my honey without knowing it was mine,

22
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:39,630
and Dai-chan caught him.

23
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:42,030
S-So...

24
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,220
Whatever.

25
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:52,540
It's not like I can tell if it's true.

26
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:57,020
That's not fair...

27
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,720
What about you?

28
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:02,050
Why didn't you say anything?

29
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,330
Huh?

30
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:09,240
If you were upset, you could've just said so.

31
00:02:10,762 --> 00:02:13,252
Why keep quiet about it?

32
00:02:21,206 --> 00:02:23,330
Well, that's...

33
00:02:26,542 --> 00:02:28,091
What?

34
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:34,160
Never mind.

35
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,750
Harutora.

36
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:28,980
Harutora.

37
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,970
There he is!

38
00:03:31,970 --> 00:03:34,224
- Sui!
- Did you really get a boyfriend?

39
00:03:34,224 --> 00:03:36,370
- Huh?
- How did you two get together?

40
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:37,480
Is he older?

41
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,257
Wait, is he from the dorm?

42
00:03:40,257 --> 00:03:42,417
What are you talking about?

43
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,150
Your date's today, right?

44
00:03:46,150 --> 00:03:49,120
This outfit doesn't show your figure.

45
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,659
At least unbutton it.

46
00:03:50,659 --> 00:03:53,650
- I'm fine with this!
- Come on!

47
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,980
It's not our fault
if he doesn't like your look!

48
00:03:55,980 --> 00:04:00,260
I heard gay couples don't last long,
so don't get too attached!

49
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:04,800
- Sui...
- Why won't he tell us?

50
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,688
[Harutora: Let's call it off for today.]

51
00:04:09,688 --> 00:04:11,058
[Yeah, sure.]

52
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:27,312
[What if a gay couple is outed?
1. Reactions vary by person and environment]

53
00:04:27,312 --> 00:04:29,440
[2. The general situation in Japan
3. Potential risks]

54
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,920
We have to be careful.

55
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:41,237
[Decide on a sign to use
for secretly checking each other's feelings.]

56
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,130
A sign, huh?

57
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,750
This works.

58
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:14,080
It's no good.

59
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,330
What's up?

60
00:05:17,790 --> 00:05:19,830
The zipper broke.

61
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:23,247
Yeah, this is done for.

62
00:05:23,247 --> 00:05:24,740
Gotta replace the whole thing.

63
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:26,210
Seriously?

64
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,450
Do you know where we can get one?

65
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:32,100
There's a craft store
at the shopping arcade by the station.

66
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,575
Someone around here probably knows.

67
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:41,383
Sui, I'm heading out for my lesson.

68
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:42,540
- Do your best.
- I'm off.

69
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,170
Have a good one.

70
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:49,560
Hey Sui, Harutora needs some help.

71
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:52,669
His zipper broke or something.
Can you come help?

72
00:05:52,669 --> 00:05:54,009
Sure.

73
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,860
You've been to the craft store.
Show him where it is.

74
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,420
Huh? Oh, sure.

75
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:01,560
Perfect timing.

76
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:04,647
- Thanks.
- No problem.

77
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:18,730
This broke, huh? And it's your favorite too.

78
00:06:20,030 --> 00:06:22,060
Sorry about this.

79
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:24,455
No, don't worry about it.

80
00:06:24,455 --> 00:06:26,670
Okay, let's get ready and head out.

81
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:28,990
Wait here. I'll be right back.

82
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:38,980
Maybe this one?

83
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:42,620
I think it's good.

84
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,230
Okay.

85
00:06:45,525 --> 00:06:47,365
Thank you.

86
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:04,220
Sui, look at this.

87
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,556
This one looks like you.

88
00:07:10,556 --> 00:07:12,939
Isn't it a bit big?

89
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:37,095
[2. The general situation in Japan
3. Potential risks]

90
00:07:47,850 --> 00:07:49,950
How about this one?

91
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:53,270
I think it's cute.

92
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:54,760
Really?

93
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,600
In that case...

94
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,790
Sorry.

95
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:22,967
Why?

96
00:08:23,941 --> 00:08:26,992
We're dating, right?

97
00:08:26,992 --> 00:08:30,840
W-We are, but...

98
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:33,250
I don't know...

99
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:39,677
I guess I'm just scared
that someone from school...

100
00:08:39,677 --> 00:08:41,920
sees us.

101
00:08:46,190 --> 00:08:47,700
Sorry.

102
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:56,100
We were enjoying our time together,
and yet...

103
00:09:04,950 --> 00:09:06,330
Here.

104
00:09:08,450 --> 00:09:09,850
Huh?

105
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:19,150
If we can't hold hands, pretend this is me.

106
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,260
Why?

107
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:29,100
Because your hands were cold.

108
00:09:33,002 --> 00:09:34,635
Thank you.

109
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:40,810
Since we're here,
let's check out a few more shops.

110
00:09:40,810 --> 00:09:42,170
Okay.

111
00:09:45,650 --> 00:09:47,310
Sui!

112
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:52,110
Whoa, this is crazy.
We haven't met since middle school.

113
00:09:52,110 --> 00:09:54,330
Oh, y-yeah.

114
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:58,610
That's some reaction!
It's me, Hikaru! You forgot?

115
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:01,010
No way. Of course I remember.

116
00:10:01,010 --> 00:10:02,460
I remember.

117
00:10:03,988 --> 00:10:05,060
Hello!

118
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,273
I'm Hikaru Takahashi.

119
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:10,490
Sui and I were classmates
for all of middle school.

120
00:10:10,490 --> 00:10:13,260
And you are?

121
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,880
- I'm...
- He's my junior.

122
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,040
Harutora, my former dorm roommate.

123
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:24,849
Oh, a dorm!
No wonder I never see you around town.

124
00:10:24,849 --> 00:10:27,539
Yeah, I haven't been back lately.

125
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,630
Remember that guy?
Matsushita, from the animal care committee?

126
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:33,122
Oh yeah, I remember him!

127
00:10:33,122 --> 00:10:34,520
Nostalgic, right?

128
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:37,230
I actually ran into him back home.

129
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:41,720
Catch you later!

130
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,450
See you.

131
00:10:47,762 --> 00:10:52,202
Sorry I left you out of the conversation.

132
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:57,025
You seemed different than usual, Sui.

133
00:10:57,025 --> 00:11:01,580
Really? But he's just a normal friend.

134
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:04,970
But you seemed flustered.

135
00:11:04,970 --> 00:11:07,890
What? That's not...

136
00:11:08,930 --> 00:11:12,620
Are you really just friends?

137
00:11:24,070 --> 00:11:25,600
Sorry.

138
00:11:28,483 --> 00:11:34,503
He was my crush in middle school.

139
00:11:36,450 --> 00:11:39,520
But it was only a little crush,

140
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:42,780
and now there's nothing at all between us.

141
00:11:43,866 --> 00:11:48,356
But you only introduced me
as a junior you roomed with.

142
00:11:58,963 --> 00:12:00,583
I'm sorry.

143
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:04,570
I know how things spread in a small town.

144
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:17,620
Hikaru.

145
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:21,680
Sui? What's up?

146
00:12:24,515 --> 00:12:25,995
You see...

147
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:36,190
The person I was with earlier...

148
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,920
My boyfriend.

149
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:44,700
Huh?

150
00:12:47,505 --> 00:12:49,585
He's my boyfriend.

151
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:05,130
Yeah, I kind of figured.

152
00:13:05,130 --> 00:13:08,990
I mean, you never seemed interested in girls.

153
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:10,400
Yeah.

154
00:13:12,024 --> 00:13:14,194
Thanks for telling me.

155
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:19,988
I actually haven't told my parents yet.

156
00:13:19,988 --> 00:13:21,510
Got it, got it.

157
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:25,589
I won't say a word. Don't worry, okay?

158
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,020
Thanks.

159
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:30,510
Now go back to him.

160
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:32,808
- Okay.
- See you.

161
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,900
I finally said it...

162
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,659
I'm sorry.

163
00:13:58,543 --> 00:14:00,143
Harutora...

164
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:12,730
After we stopped rooming together,

165
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:19,140
I couldn't calm down
unless I was doing something.

166
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,300
It hurt.

167
00:14:28,214 --> 00:14:30,774
<i>It hurt so much.</i>

168
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:36,110
What were you doing in the rain?

169
00:14:36,110 --> 00:14:37,790
Running.

170
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,910
What happened to you?

171
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:44,010
You've been acting weird.

172
00:14:44,810 --> 00:14:47,360
Do you drop dead if you're not moving?

173
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:51,830
Of course not.

174
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:53,950
You worry too much.

175
00:14:54,670 --> 00:14:57,140
Sorry for worrying, then!

176
00:14:58,430 --> 00:15:00,430
It's because I know how hard you work,

177
00:15:00,430 --> 00:15:04,620
and how much you love basketball, idiot.

178
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:25,390
I can't be apart from Sui.

179
00:15:27,007 --> 00:15:31,417
If I'm not moving, I'll die.

180
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,740
When I felt down...

181
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:50,279
hearing you warmly saying, "welcome home"...

182
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:54,190
would lift my spirits.

183
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,571
Even when we lost a game,

184
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:09,580
you stayed by my side without saying a word.

185
00:16:13,432 --> 00:16:16,162
I'd sleep on the floor on purpose...

186
00:16:18,409 --> 00:16:21,339
because I loved having you fuss over me.

187
00:16:26,741 --> 00:16:28,911
I wanted you near me.

188
00:16:36,269 --> 00:16:38,179
I see.

189
00:16:42,641 --> 00:16:48,390
I never thought
you were hurting that badly.

190
00:16:48,390 --> 00:16:51,000
I can feel the love.

191
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:57,050
Sorry, no filter.

192
00:16:57,050 --> 00:17:01,770
No, it's fine. You can be honest.

193
00:17:05,590 --> 00:17:07,150
Just me?

194
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:10,316
Huh?

195
00:17:11,090 --> 00:17:15,890
Why won't you ever be honest with me?

196
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:20,420
No, how I feel doesn't really matter.

197
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:24,500
You always put yourself last.

198
00:17:25,910 --> 00:17:28,430
There are more important things.

199
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:33,034
Shouldn't you usually...

200
00:17:34,516 --> 00:17:36,990
focus on yourself first?

201
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:48,710
But if I say something childish,
that would be a burden to you.

202
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:53,640
Huh?

203
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,440
Harutora, you're probably...

204
00:18:03,150 --> 00:18:06,470
not as grown-up as you think you are.

205
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:09,980
Huh?

206
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:13,080
I mean, you have a quick temper.

207
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:19,630
I thought I was mature.

208
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:25,510
I even took care of my younger siblings.

209
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:30,200
No, no way.

210
00:18:31,770 --> 00:18:33,950
Are you serious?

211
00:18:35,016 --> 00:18:36,646
Oh, man...

212
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,110
It's okay to be a kid.

213
00:18:54,410 --> 00:18:55,800
Huh?

214
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:02,600
We're going to grow up from here on out.

215
00:19:05,290 --> 00:19:07,020
From here on out?

216
00:19:07,910 --> 00:19:09,580
Grow up?

217
00:19:10,690 --> 00:19:12,590
Harutora!

218
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:13,990
Harutora, let's play.

219
00:19:13,990 --> 00:19:17,240
Harutora, let's play. Let's go to the park.

220
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:24,927
<i>I used to think
I always had to be the big brother.</i>

221
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:29,290
Being lonely...

222
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,800
Wanting to be spoiled...

223
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:44,630
Those kinds of things felt better off unsaid.

224
00:19:46,524 --> 00:19:48,870
Harutora.

225
00:19:48,870 --> 00:19:50,270
But...

226
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,400
It's okay to say it, huh?

227
00:19:55,630 --> 00:19:57,010
What?

228
00:20:01,771 --> 00:20:03,231
I...

229
00:20:20,363 --> 00:20:22,933
I was so lonely.

230
00:21:38,810 --> 00:21:40,300
This is...

231
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:45,160
No, wait!

232
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:53,440
When I finished it,
I thought it looked great.

233
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:56,748
But when I tried to give it to you,
I kept noticing flaws.

234
00:22:02,330 --> 00:22:05,220
You were going to the craft store...

235
00:22:05,220 --> 00:22:09,320
I was worried about what would happen
if our relationship got out,

236
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:16,630
so I read that you could use a sign
to confirm your love for each other.

237
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:23,340
Even when we're apart,
my feelings are always right by your side.

238
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:29,270
Sorry. That was kind of heavy, huh?

239
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:34,610
Not at all.

240
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:41,920
I'll cherish this forever.

